span class="font-heading text-[1.2rem] font-semibold leading-snug tracking-[-0.025em] text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-ember sm:text-[1.4rem]">Is it safe to open the door with a broken spring?</span><span class="flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border transition-[background-color,border-color,color,transform,translate,scale,rotate] duration-500 ease-expo rotate-45 border-ink bg-ink text-cream" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-plus size-4"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="M12 5v14"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div id="_R_b3b6_-a-0" role="region" aria-labelledby="_R_b3b6_-q-0" class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,opacity] duration-500 ease-expo grid-rows-[1fr] opacity-100"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="max-w-2xl pb-7 pr-14 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-slate">No. The spring carries the door&#x27;s weight, so without it the opener strains and the door can come down hard. If the door is closed, pull the red cord to disconnect the opener, leave the door shut and give us a call.</p></div></div></div><div class="border-b border-ink/10"><h3><button id="_R_b3b6_-q-1" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="_R_b3b6_-a-1" class="group flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-6 py-6 text-left"><span class="font-heading text-[1.2rem] font-semibold leading-snug tracking-[-0.025em] text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-ember sm:text-[1.4rem]">Is there a call-out fee?</span><span class="flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border transition-[background-color,border-color,color,transform,translate,scale,rotate] duration-500 ease-expo border-ink/15 text-ink group-hover:border-ink/40" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-plus size-4"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="M12 5v14"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div id="_R_b3b6_-a-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="_R_b3b6_-q-1" class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,opacity] duration-500 ease-expo grid-rows-[0fr] opacity-0"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="max-w-2xl pb-7 pr-14 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-slate">A $59 diagnostic fee applies, and it is waived when we carry out the repair. You&#x27;ll hear about it before we set off, never after.</p></div></div></div><div class="border-b border-ink/10"><h3><button id="_R_b3b6_-q-2" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="_R_b3b6_-a-2" class="group flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-6 py-6 text-left"><span class="font-heading text-[1.2rem] font-semibold leading-snug tracking-[-0.025em] text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-ember sm:text-[1.4rem]">Only one spring broke. Why change both?</span><span class="flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border transition-[background-color,border-color,color,transform,translate,scale,rotate] duration-500 ease-expo border-ink/15 text-ink group-hover:border-ink/40" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-plus size-4"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="M12 5v14"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div id="_R_b3b6_-a-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="_R_b3b6_-q-2" class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,opacity] duration-500 ease-expo grid-rows-[0fr] opacity-0"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="max-w-2xl pb-7 pr-14 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-slate">The pair went in together and has done exactly the same number of cycles. The second one usually gives out within months, so replacing both saves you another visit.</p></div></div></div><div class="border-b border-ink/10"><h3><button id="_R_b3b6_-q-3" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="_R_b3b6_-a-3" class="group flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-6 py-6 text-left"><span class="font-heading text-[1.2rem] font-semibold leading-snug tracking-[-0.025em] text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-ember sm:text-[1.4rem]">How long does a new door take from start to finish?</span><span class="flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border transition-[background-color,border-color,color,transform,translate,scale,rotate] duration-500 ease-expo border-ink/15 text-ink group-hover:border-ink/40" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-plus size-4"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="M12 5v14"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div id="_R_b3b6_-a-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="_R_b3b6_-q-3" class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,opacity] duration-500 ease-expo grid-rows-[0fr] opacity-0"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="max-w-2xl pb-7 pr-14 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-slate">The measure takes around 20 minutes. Most doors arrive within 1–3 weeks, and fitting takes 4–6 hours including taking the old door away.</p></div></div></div><div class="border-b border-ink/10"><h3><button id="_R_b3b6_-q-4" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="_R_b3b6_-a-4" class="group flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-6 py-6 text-left"><span class="font-heading text-[1.2rem] font-semibold leading-snug tracking-[-0.025em] text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-ember sm:text-[1.4rem]">Which opener brands can you repair?</span><span class="flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border transition-[background-color,border-color,color,transform,translate,scale,rotate] duration-500 ease-expo border-ink/15 text-ink group-hover:border-ink/40" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-plus size-4"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="M12 5v14"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div id="_R_b3b6_-a-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="_R_b3b6_-q-4" class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,opacity] duration-500 ease-expo grid-rows-[0fr] opacity-0"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="max-w-2xl pb-7 pr-14 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-slate">Every major residential brand, older models included. If the parts for yours are no longer made, we&#x27;ll say so on the spot.</p></div></div></div><div class="border-b border-ink/10"><h3><button id="_R_b3b6_-q-5" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="_R_b3b6_-a-5" class="group flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-6 py-6 text-left"><span class="font-heading text-[1.2rem] font-semibold leading-snug tracking-[-0.025em] text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-ember sm:text-[1.4rem]">Can you come out at the weekend?</span><span class="flex size-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border transition-[background-color,border-color,color,transform,translate,scale,rotate] duration-500 ease-expo border-ink/15 text-ink group-hover:border-ink/40" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-plus size-4"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="M12 5v14"></path></svg></span></button></h3><div id="_R_b3b6_-a-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="_R_b3b6_-q-5" class="grid transition-[grid-template-rows,opacity] duration-500 ease-expo grid-rows-[0fr] opacity-0"><div class="overflow-hidden"><p class="max-w-2xl pb-7 pr-14 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-slate">Yes, on Saturdays from 8 AM to 6 PM. The emergency line runs every day until 10 PM.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><section id="quote" class="bg-sand/60 py-24 md:py-32"><div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[1360px] px-5 sm:px-6 md:px-8 xl:px-10 grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-10"><div class="lg:col-span-5"><div class="lg:sticky lg:top-32"><div class="flex flex-col gap-6"><div><p class="inline-flex items-center gap-2.5 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ember"><span class="size-1.5 rotate-45 bg-ember" aria-hidden="true"></span>Get a price</p><h2 class="mt-5 text-h2 font-semibold text-balance text-ink max-w-[15ch]">Describe the door. Get your price by text.</h2></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-6"><div class="max-w-xl text-lead text-pretty text-slate">Only the questions your job calls for, nothing extra. Someone on our team replies in about 30 minutes during business hours.</div></div></div><div class="mt-10"><ol class="space-y-0"><li class="flex gap-5 border-t border-ink/10 py-5"><span class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink font-mono text-[12px] text-cream">1</span><span class="pt-1.5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-ink">A price range arrives by text.</span></li><li class="flex gap-5 border-t border-ink/10 py-5"><span class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink font-mono text-[12px] text-cream">2</span><span class="pt-1.5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-ink">You choose the visit window.</span></li><li class="flex gap-5 border-t border-ink/10 py-5"><span class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink font-mono text-[12px] text-cream">3</span><span class="pt-1.5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-ink">Before any work begins, your technician confirms the exact price on site.</span></li></ol></div><a href="tel:5555550148" class="group mt-8 flex items-center gap-4 rounded-[22px] bg-i